  "prefLabel": "Dec 204.13 Quorum",
  "priorExpiration": "2001-03-17",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Dec 204.13 Quorum.\n\n(a) Five members of the committee shall constitute a quorum for the purpose of holding and conducting a hearing.\n\n(b) If a quorum of 5 members of the committee is lacking, then 4 members of the committee shall constitute a quorum for the purpose of holding and conducting the hearing, provided that a decision of the committee shall be made by a quorum of the committee after a review of the transcript and exhibits presented at the hearing by the committee members who did not attend the hearing.\n\nSource. #4235, eff 2-20-87, EXPIRED: 2-20-93\n\nNew. #5700, INTERIM, eff 9-17-93, EXPIRED: 1-15-94\n\nNew. #5824, eff 8-30-94, EXPIRED: 8-30-00\n\nNew. #7366, INTERIM, eff 9-18-00, EXPIRED: 3-17-01\n\nNew. #9144-A eff 4-25-08",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/dec100-200.html"
